00:30:17,048 --> 00:30:20,464
In those 12 years,
I've been a good soldier.

481
00:30:20,677 --> 00:30:23,713
And I've denied what
every nerve ending in my body

482
00:30:23,930 --> 00:30:25,674
is telling me is more real than not.

483
00:30:25,890 --> 00:30:28,179
I've had one dream,
not variations on a dream,

484
00:30:28,393 --> 00:30:29,971
the same dream.
Night after night...

485
00:30:30,187 --> 00:30:33,223
No. No. I'm sorry.

486
00:30:33,440 --> 00:30:35,896
You're saying that an entire squad
of U.S. Army soldiers

487
00:30:36,109 --> 00:30:38,019
was hypnotized into believing
that Raymond Shaw

488
00:30:38,236 --> 00:30:39,814
deserved the Medal of Honor.

489
00:30:40,113 --> 00:30:42,735
And that somehow,
thanks to your dream,

490
00:30:42,950 --> 00:30:45,488
you're the only one
who knows the truth.

491
00:30:46,245 --> 00:30:49,281
Major Marco, you will stay clear
of Congressman Shaw.

492
00:30:54,837 --> 00:30:57,707
And you are to resume
your medication.

493
00:30:57,923 --> 00:30:59,797
That is an order.

494
00:31:00,009 --> 00:31:01,551
That will be all, major.

495
00:31:02,261 --> 00:31:05,262
<i>Somewhere right now, an
American soldier in the war on terror</i>

496
00:31:05,473 --> 00:31:07,798
<i>is worried about his
family back home.</i>

497
00:31:08,559 --> 00:31:11,596
<i>Somewhere right now,
in some small American town,</i>

498
00:31:11,812 --> 00:31:14,564
<i>his grandmother is standing
in her kitchen.</i>

499
00:31:14,774 --> 00:31:17,347
<i>She's got her medicine bottle
in one hand,</i>

500
00:31:17,568 --> 00:31:20,937
<i>she's opening the refrigerator
with the other and she's thinking:</i>

501
00:31:21,906 --> 00:31:24,195
<i>"I can pay for my medicine...</i>

502
00:31:25,243 --> 00:31:27,401
<i>...or I can pay for my dinner.</i>

503
00:31:28,329 --> 00:31:30,405
<i>I can't do both. "</i>

504
00:31:30,957 --> 00:31:32,877
<i>I don't believe that our mothers
and grandmothers</i>

505
00:31:32,959 --> 00:31:36,044
<i>should have to face that kind of
decision, not in this country.</i>

506
00:31:38,131 --> 00:31:41,251
<i>I don't believe that the brave men
and women of our armed forces,</i>

507
00:31:41,468 --> 00:31:44,041
<i>risking their lives overseas,
should have to worry</i>

508
00:31:44,846 --> 00:31:48,381
<i>about their families back here
in America.</i>

509
00:31:49,476 --> 00:31:51,682
<i>You see, there are some gaps
in this country...</i>

510
00:31:52,896 --> 00:31:55,767
<i>...deep chasms
that we need to bridge.</i>

511
00:31:57,609 --> 00:31:59,401
<i>The gap between rich and poor,</i>

512
00:31:59,778 --> 00:32:03,112
<i>between government
and the people,</i>

513
00:32:03,324 --> 00:32:06,693
<i>between true security
and the notion of feeling safe.</i>

514
00:32:06,911 --> 00:32:09,117
Second floor, room three,
end of hall.

515
00:32:09,622 --> 00:32:12,113
<i>Between what is real...</i>

516
00:32:12,333 --> 00:32:13,792
Don't you just love this guy?

517
00:32:14,001 --> 00:32:15,661
<i>And what is not.</i>

518
00:32:16,796 --> 00:32:19,465
<i>Tough choices are an unavoidable
element of leadership,</i>

519
00:32:19,674 --> 00:32:22,247
<i>I would just urge the governor
to remember that</i>

520
00:32:22,468 --> 00:32:26,003
<i>the primary responsibility
of government...</i>

521
00:32:48,536 --> 00:32:50,280
Al Melvin.

522
00:32:52,541 --> 00:32:55,210
Al, it's Ben Marco.
Are you in there?

523
00:33:00,465 --> 00:33:02,375
Fox is in the henhouse.

524
00:33:02,592 --> 00:33:04,336
Weasel.

525
00:33:05,429 --> 00:33:08,845
Weasel is...

526
00:33:10,476 --> 00:33:12,634
The weasel is a weasel.

527
00:33:14,313 --> 00:33:16,021
Sir, I'll be right outside.

528
00:33:16,774 --> 00:33:17,769
What?

529
00:33:18,484 --> 00:33:20,642
I'll be right outside, sir.

530
00:33:21,487 --> 00:33:22,862
I know.

531
00:33:23,572 --> 00:33:26,110
- Good night.
- Good night, sir.

532
00:33:27,368 --> 00:33:29,360
- Shall I get that for you, sir?
- No.

533
00:33:29,578 --> 00:33:31,701
- Good night, sir.
- Good night.

534
00:33:54,270 --> 00:33:56,559
You have 30 seconds, Mother.

535
00:33:56,773 --> 00:33:58,148
Am I that predictable?

536
00:33:58,441 --> 00:34:00,351
You have no idea.

537
00:34:00,610 --> 00:34:03,315
I'm calling to compliment you,
Mr. Grumpy.

538
00:34:03,530 --> 00:34:06,484
I thought you were
magnificent tonight.

539
00:34:06,741 --> 00:34:09,659
And so did all the network
campaign experts.

540
00:34:10,203 --> 00:34:13,738
<i>And that compassionate
vigilance thing</i>

541
00:34:13,957 --> 00:34:16,709
<i>is working quite well for you.</i>

542
00:34:17,419 --> 00:34:20,420
- I might have to convert.
- I happen to believe in it.

543
00:34:20,631 --> 00:34:22,089
<i>Oh, yes, of course you do.</i>

544
00:34:22,299 --> 00:34:24,042
<i>- Now, Raymond...</i>
- Good night, Mother.

545
00:34:24,593 --> 00:34:26,918
<i>Raymond? What? No, wait, wait.</i>

546
00:34:28,555 --> 00:34:30,762
- Hang on a second.
<i>- What? Raymond?</i>

547
00:34:31,267 --> 00:34:32,512
Are you there?

548
00:34:35,187 --> 00:34:36,598
Yes?

549
00:34:36,981 --> 00:34:38,808
<i>Sergeant Shaw?</i>

550
00:34:39,233 --> 00:34:40,941
Who is this?

551
00:34:41,652 --> 00:34:44,772
<i>- Sergeant Raymond Shaw?</i>
- Yes.

552
00:34:45,114 --> 00:34:47,687
<i>Raymond Prentiss Shaw?</i>

553
00:34:52,955 --> 00:34:54,450
Yes.

554
00:34:54,749 --> 00:34:56,077
<i>Listen.</i>

555
00:34:56,668 --> 00:34:58,791
<i>Go to the bedroom of your suite.</i>

556
00:34:59,420 --> 00:35:02,125
<i>Enter the hallway there.</i>

557
00:35:02,340 --> 00:35:05,923
<i>Go to the end and open the closet.</i>

558
00:35:35,207 --> 00:35:37,413
Yes, thank you.

559
00:35:40,045 --> 00:35:42,619
- Hello, Raymond.
- Hello.

560
00:35:42,881 --> 00:35:44,708
Do you remember me?

561
00:35:49,430 --> 00:35:50,889
No, sir, I don't.

562
00:35:51,182 --> 00:35:53,720
Brilliant. We've got 20 minutes
for our little checkup

563
00:35:53,934 --> 00:35:56,770
from the neck up, gentlemen,
so if we could take his jacket.

564
00:35:56,979 --> 00:35:58,473
Please sit down.

565
00:36:01,901 --> 00:36:04,522
No, Mr. Villalobos, I'm just...
The Army's got me gathering

566
00:36:04,737 --> 00:36:07,655
information on stress disorders,
so I'm just...

567
00:36:07,907 --> 00:36:11,276
...you know, just running statistics,
trying to find out about my old team...

568
00:36:15,123 --> 00:36:17,115
Well, listen. Mr. Wilson,

569
00:36:17,375 --> 00:36:21,871
when Nathan came home,
was he preoccupied with Kuwait?

570
00:36:22,088 --> 00:36:23,808
I mean, did he have nightmares
or bad dreams

571
00:36:23,923 --> 00:36:25,631
about the firefight over there?

572
00:36:30,430 --> 00:36:35,057
You'll feel a little cold
as this anesthetic gel goes on.

573
00:36:40,065 --> 00:36:42,307
Probe sheath...

574
00:36:42,526 --> 00:36:45,361
...and probe.

575
00:36:48,949 --> 00:36:51,405
Please relax.
Are you relaxed, Raymond?

576
00:36:51,618 --> 00:36:52,733
Yes, sir.

577
00:36:52,995 --> 00:36:57,740
Now, Raymond, I am going to drill
a tiny hole in the skull,

578
00:36:57,958 --> 00:37:01,826
which will allow delivery
of the new implant.

579
00:37:02,463 --> 00:37:05,499
So, what you'll feel is a little
discomfort in the form of pressure

580
00:37:05,716 --> 00:37:08,088
and also a loud vibrating noise
in your head,

581
00:37:08,302 --> 00:37:12,252
all of which, of course,
is completely normal.

582
00:39:14,431 --> 00:39:15,712
<i>Thank you.</i>

583
00:39:18,435 --> 00:39:21,223
Of course, as soon as this
or any task is completed,

584
00:39:21,438 --> 00:39:26,350
you will already have forgotten
that it ever actually took place.

585
00:39:27,278 --> 00:39:29,235
Probe going in now.

586
00:39:39,123 --> 00:39:40,404
Good.

587
00:39:42,210 --> 00:39:44,001
Excellent.

588
00:39:44,212 --> 00:39:46,619
Releasing implant.

589
00:39:46,839 --> 00:39:49,330
There. That wasn't so bad,
was it, Raymond?

590
00:39:49,550 --> 00:39:50,831
No, sir.

591
00:39:51,511 --> 00:39:53,800
That's good. No decay, no slippage.

592
00:39:54,013 --> 00:39:58,225
Everything seems to be
in flawless working condition.

593
00:40:24,086 --> 00:40:25,995
Now, Raymond.

594
00:40:26,255 --> 00:40:29,790
Can you remember the deaths
of Private Baker and Private Ingram?

595
00:40:30,009 --> 00:40:31,004
Yes, sir.

596
00:40:31,260 --> 00:40:33,751
Good. Can you describe them
for me, please?

597
00:40:33,971 --> 00:40:37,007
<i>We're on a routine recon
inside Iraqi-controlled terrain,</i>

598
00:40:37,224 --> 00:40:39,715
<i>assessing troop strength.</i>

599
00:40:41,187 --> 00:40:45,516
"We're on a routine recon
inside Iraqi-controlled terrain,

600
00:40:45,733 --> 00:40:47,108
assessing troop strength."

601
00:40:47,318 --> 00:40:49,939
The mission ends without incident.
We're heading back...

602
00:40:50,154 --> 00:40:52,906
"Toward the command.
The night is clear. Stars..."

603
00:40:53,157 --> 00:40:56,491
The night is clear.
Stars, but no moon.

604
00:40:57,078 --> 00:40:58,323
<i>The patrol is ambushed.</i>

605
00:40:58,538 --> 00:41:01,788
<i>We're engaged unexpectedly by
ground forces with helicopter support.</i>

606
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:04,835
<i>RPG incoming, mortar fire.</i>

607
00:41:05,170 --> 00:41:06,712
"Captain..."

608
00:41:08,339 --> 00:41:10,665
Captain Marco
is knocked unconscious.

609
00:41:10,884 --> 00:41:14,798
In the ensuing firefight, Eddie Ingram
gets himself separated to the left.

610
00:41:15,555 --> 00:41:17,678
<i>Baker goes after him.</i>

611
00:41:17,891 --> 00:41:20,014
<i>An incoming mortar shell
kills them both instantly</i>

612
00:41:20,227 --> 00:41:23,643
<i>before I am able to locate and
eliminate the source of the ordnance.</i>

613
00:41:25,482 --> 00:41:28,851
<i>Captain. Captain Marco.</i>

614
00:41:29,069 --> 00:41:30,480
<i>Help me.</i>

615
00:41:38,203 --> 00:41:41,038
Pardon me. Is this seat taken?

616
00:41:41,665 --> 00:41:45,200
I see the captain enjoys
the road less traveled.

617
00:42:02,687 --> 00:42:04,726
Paper or plastic?

618
00:42:06,774 --> 00:42:10,024
Oh, come on.
From the grocery store.

619
00:42:10,236 --> 00:42:13,237
You know, at the checkout stand.
Paper or plastic girl, that's me.

620
00:42:13,448 --> 00:42:14,906
"Paper or plastic, sir?"

621
00:42:16,576 --> 00:42:17,987
I see you there all the time.

622
00:42:18,203 --> 00:42:20,694
Bennett Marco.
Checks from First National Bank.

623
00:42:20,914 --> 00:42:25,706
Romance novels, instant noodles,
NoDoz and tomatoes.

624
00:42:29,798 --> 00:42:32,585
So anyway, I'm on vacation.

625
00:42:32,801 --> 00:42:34,959
Holiday in the Big Apple
and all of that.

626
00:42:35,178 --> 00:42:37,586
And I saw you sitting here
and I said, "Hey,

627
00:42:37,806 --> 00:42:40,677
why not reach out
and touch someone?"

628
00:42:44,479 --> 00:42:47,397
So, what, I suppose
you're heading to New York City.

629
00:42:47,608 --> 00:42:49,731
Yeah, yeah, I'm... Yeah.

630
00:42:50,360 --> 00:42:52,768
Business? Pleasure? Both?

631
00:42:53,113 --> 00:42:58,108
Well, I'm just... I got an old friend
up there, an old Army friend that...

632
00:42:59,078 --> 00:43:01,948
Well, he's in politics now
and I'm just gonna

633
00:43:02,164 --> 00:43:04,489
catch up on old times with him.

634
00:43:08,462 --> 00:43:10,040
I'm sorry, you said your name was?

635
00:43:10,965 --> 00:43:12,376
Eugenie.

636
00:43:13,384 --> 00:43:14,962
What do your friends call you?

637
00:43:15,178 --> 00:43:17,301
My friends, they call me Rosie.

638
00:43:17,763 --> 00:43:19,756
- Rosie?
- Yeah, see, my full name is

639
00:43:19,974 --> 00:43:21,654
Eugenie Rose.
I like the Rosie part better.

640
00:43:21,726 --> 00:43:24,478
Eugenie is, well...

641
00:43:25,021 --> 00:43:26,563
...fragile.

642
00:43:26,940 --> 00:43:30,143
Yeah, but still, when I asked you
your name, you didn't say...

643
00:43:30,610 --> 00:43:32,484
What did you say?
You said Eugenie.

644
00:43:32,695 --> 00:43:34,854
Yeah, well...

645
00:43:35,448 --> 00:43:40,157
...maybe I was feeling fragile
at the time.

646
00:43:49,463 --> 00:43:50,921
Are you okay?

647
00:43:51,131 --> 00:43:52,459
Excuse me.

648
00:44:40,598 --> 00:44:42,009
Hello, captain.

649
00:44:42,767 --> 00:44:44,178
Do you remember me?

650
00:45:16,427 --> 00:45:17,755
Ben.

651
00:45:18,637 --> 00:45:22,089
Hey. I'm gonna get a cab.
You want me to drop you somewhere?

652
00:45:22,308 --> 00:45:23,506
No, I'm okay.

653
00:45:23,726 --> 00:45:25,646
Okay. So your friend's
gonna meet you here, then?

654
00:45:25,728 --> 00:45:27,103
No.

655
00:45:28,647 --> 00:45:30,058
All right.

656
00:45:30,274 --> 00:45:33,275
El Dorado 5-9970.

657
00:45:35,696 --> 00:45:39,480
It's my cell phone number,
in case you ever... You know.

658
00:45:39,700 --> 00:45:41,693
I like to say it the old-fashioned way.

659
00:45:41,911 --> 00:45:45,280
Can you remember or should I write it
on your chest with a Sharpie?

660
00:45:46,165 --> 00:45:48,372
- I'll remember.
- Okay.

661
00:45:49,085 --> 00:45:51,410
Hey, you're kind of...

662
00:45:52,088 --> 00:45:54,579
You need somewhere to go
to freshen up?

663
00:45:56,384 --> 00:45:58,044
<i>Pentagon watchdogs
today accused</i>

664
00:45:58,261 --> 00:46:00,633
<i>the private equity fund
Manchurian Global</i>

665
00:46:00,847 --> 00:46:04,679
<i>of grossly overpricing plasma
and other critical medical supplies</i>

666
00:46:04,893 --> 00:46:06,969
<i>during the recent
Indonesian incursion,</i>

667
00:46:07,187 --> 00:46:11,481
<i>even as the company secured
a half-billion-dollar no-bid contract</i>

668
00:46:11,691 --> 00:46:14,811
<i>to provide combat support services
to American soldiers</i>

669
00:46:15,028 --> 00:46:17,187
<i>preparing to mobilize in Sri Lanka.</i>

670
00:46:29,710 --> 00:46:31,501
There you go.

671
00:46:32,338 --> 00:46:33,666
Come on in.

672
00:46:33,881 --> 00:46:36,454
This is my cousin's apartment.

673
00:46:36,884 --> 00:46:38,793
- Is she here?
- No.

674
00:46:39,011 --> 00:46:41,051
Be it ever so humble.

675
00:46:41,472 --> 00:46:43,678
No place like home, right?

676
00:46:43,933 --> 00:46:47,136
Believe it or not, there's a view.

677
00:46:47,353 --> 00:46:50,437
Go to the fire escape
and tilt your head up,

678
00:46:50,690 --> 00:46:52,848
you can almost see a tree.

679
00:46:55,027 --> 00:46:57,316
- Can I get you something to drink?
- No, I'm fine.

680
00:46:59,949 --> 00:47:02,701
I've got some dieter's tea.

681
00:47:02,910 --> 00:47:06,529
It's great for your metabolism,
if you're into that.

682
00:47:06,748 --> 00:47:11,706
Or some tomato juice. No? All right.

683
00:47:12,420 --> 00:47:14,045
Or...

684
00:47:14,255 --> 00:47:15,370
...some water?

685
00:47:15,840 --> 00:47:17,963
- No, thank you.
- I'm sorry.

686
00:47:19,094 --> 00:47:21,549
I'm nervous.
I yak when I get nervous.

687
00:47:22,681 --> 00:47:24,424
Where is she, your cousin?

688
00:47:25,767 --> 00:47:27,724
She's on tour with <i>Dreamgirls</i>.

689
00:47:39,031 --> 00:47:40,229
Hey, are you okay?

690
00:47:42,868 --> 00:47:44,243
Yeah.

691
00:47:47,039 --> 00:47:50,075
Look, I'm sorry about
what happened earlier.

692
00:47:50,292 --> 00:47:52,830
You don't have to apologize to me.

693
00:47:53,879 --> 00:47:56,038
I'll make you some tea.

694
00:48:35,088 --> 00:48:38,588
Jesus. Where's the lemon? Okay.

695
00:48:39,301 --> 00:48:42,966
- You okay in there?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

696
00:48:43,597 --> 00:48:46,882
You know, I left you some towels
in there, did you see them?

697
00:48:50,854 --> 00:48:52,977
- What was that?
- Dropped my bag.

698
00:49:00,614 --> 00:49:02,073
Ben?

699
00:49:03,367 --> 00:49:05,158
Are you okay in there?

700
00:49:05,619 --> 00:49:06,948
Earth to Ben.

701
00:49:07,705 --> 00:49:09,033
Yeah.

702
00:49:09,331 --> 00:49:12,498
- You sure everything's all right?
- Yes.

703
00:49:15,379 --> 00:49:16,922
Ben?

704
00:49:26,349 --> 00:49:27,973
Ben?

705
00:49:28,685 --> 00:49:30,428
Ben?

706
00:49:31,354 --> 00:49:32,517
Ben.

707
00:49:37,068 --> 00:49:38,444
Ben?

708
00:50:02,052 --> 00:50:03,381
What are you doing?

709
00:50:07,766 --> 00:50:09,474
Did you see that?

710
00:50:13,272 --> 00:50:15,395
What I had in my hand.

711
00:50:19,487 --> 00:50:22,322
<i>I wasn't hallucinating, Delp.
I held it in my hand.</i>

712
00:50:22,531 --> 00:50:24,904
That's what they all say, Marco.

713
00:50:25,117 --> 00:50:28,202
Some wicked shit got sprayed
on you guys during Desert Storm.

714
00:50:28,788 --> 00:50:31,908
Besides all the depleted uranium,
I mean.

715
00:50:32,583 --> 00:50:34,623
I personally know of
a couple of Rangers

716
00:50:34,836 --> 00:50:37,587
who swear that they see only
in tertiary colors now,

717
00:50:37,797 --> 00:50:40,881
- Delp.
- And can pick up sports talk radio

718
00:50:41,092 --> 00:50:44,543
in their cortical block if they get
too close to a Con-Ed transformer.

719
00:50:44,971 --> 00:50:46,845
It's not Gulf War Syndrome.

720
00:50:53,688 --> 00:50:59,809
The Army did try this
tiny, implantable ID thing.

721
00:51:01,655 --> 00:51:04,691
You could imbed it under the skin,
then scan it like a bar code

722
00:51:04,908 --> 00:51:07,529
for medical emergency information:

723
00:51:07,995 --> 00:51:10,201
Blood type, DNA.

724
00:51:10,414 --> 00:51:12,453
Well, the Army never put one in me.

725
00:51:16,295 --> 00:51:18,537
That you know of, man.

726
00:51:21,050 --> 00:51:22,793
That you know of.

727
00:51:33,521 --> 00:51:36,806
<i>U.S. Planes bombed selected sites
in Guinea today, acting on intelligence</i>

728
00:51:37,024 --> 00:51:40,358
<i>that the African nation's military
regime had secretly resumed</i>

729
00:51:40,570 --> 00:51:42,194
<i>its chemical weapons program.</i>

730
00:51:42,405 --> 00:51:44,725
<i>The secretary of defense declined
to comment on the attack,</i>

731
00:51:44,824 --> 00:51:46,698
<i>saying only that the mission
was successful,</i>

732
00:51:46,909 --> 00:51:49,946
<i>targets acquired, that all American
personnel involved here</i>

733
00:51:50,163 --> 00:51:53,579
<i>- were home safe and sound.
- Striking transportation workers...</i>

734
00:51:54,792 --> 00:51:59,170
My dreams seem more real to me

735
00:51:59,380 --> 00:52:02,796
than what I actually remember
happening over there. It's like...

736
00:52:05,053 --> 00:52:10,474
It's like somewhere along the line
I got brainwashed or something and...

737
00:52:12,853 --> 00:52:15,604
I'm just, like, all scrambled up.

738
00:52:16,773 --> 00:52:18,813
We have all been
brainwashed, Marco.

739
00:52:20,027 --> 00:52:23,360
As for somebody
imbedding electric probes

740
00:52:23,572 --> 00:52:28,151
and computer chips in your brain
to make you do things,

741
00:52:28,410 --> 00:52:30,202
it's horseshit, man.

742
00:52:32,956 --> 00:52:34,367
A little electroshock...

743
00:52:35,334 --> 00:52:38,869
...and sleep deprivation will do
the trick for a fraction of the price.

744
00:52:39,088 --> 00:52:41,080
Ask the Uzbeks.

745
00:52:42,299 --> 00:52:44,257
What about my dreams?

746
00:52:45,594 --> 00:52:48,798
What if all this is your dream...

747
00:52:49,932 --> 00:52:52,850
...and you are really
still back in Kuwait?

748
00:53:16,793 --> 00:53:19,913
- Thanks for coming out. Thank you.
- Congressman!

749
00:53:20,130 --> 00:53:21,707
- Congressman!
- Congressman!

750
00:53:21,923 --> 00:53:24,593
Congressman! Congressman!
Why do you and Governor Arthur

751
00:53:24,801 --> 00:53:26,593
oppose deploying troops
into Indonesia?

752
00:53:26,803 --> 00:53:28,262
Well, Governor Arthur and I believe

753
00:53:28,472 --> 00:53:30,232
we can't clean up the world
with dirty hands.

754
00:53:30,390 --> 00:53:32,050
Sergeant Shaw!

755
00:53:33,810 --> 00:53:35,518
Do you ever dream about Kuwait?

756
00:53:35,854 --> 00:53:37,646
Captain Marco.

757
00:53:39,566 --> 00:53:41,310
It's okay. It's okay.

758
00:53:41,527 --> 00:53:43,021
Nice to see you, sir.

759
00:53:43,278 --> 00:53:45,651
Good evening.
It's good to see you too.

760
00:53:45,990 --> 00:53:47,448
Why did you ask me about Kuwait?

761
00:53:47,658 --> 00:53:49,218
I didn't.
I asked you about your dreams.

762
00:53:49,326 --> 00:53:50,818
- Thank you, Lily.
- Congressman Shaw, I'm sorry.

763
00:53:50,828 --> 00:53:53,348
They wanna know if you can do
an interview with Larry King at 6?

764
00:53:53,414 --> 00:53:55,094
- No, no.
- No to the interview or no to 6?

765
00:53:55,166 --> 00:53:56,766
No. He wants to talk
about my mother. No.

766
00:53:56,876 --> 00:53:58,716
- Everything under control, P. J?
- Hello, sir.

767
00:53:58,961 --> 00:54:00,621
Good to see you.

768
00:54:00,880 --> 00:54:02,837
So, captain, what can I do for you?

769
00:54:03,049 --> 00:54:04,569
I just need a few minutes
of your time.

770
00:54:04,675 --> 00:54:06,035
Congressman Shaw,
a moment, please?

771
00:54:06,177 --> 00:54:07,126
Private time.

772
00:54:07,345 --> 00:54:10,014
Unfortunately, this is as private
as it gets for me now.

773
00:54:10,223 --> 00:54:11,765
- I understand.
- He's all right, Will.

774
00:54:11,974 --> 00:54:13,967
- Come on in.
- Thank you, thank you.

775
00:54:15,520 --> 00:54:18,189
- Hey, George.
- There are these dreams

776
00:54:18,398 --> 00:54:21,149
that some of the men
from our unit have been having.

777
00:54:21,359 --> 00:54:22,687
Including you?

778
00:54:22,902 --> 00:54:24,183
Well...

779
00:54:24,821 --> 00:54:27,857
...it's more of a question
of what actually happened

780
00:54:28,074 --> 00:54:30,114
the night that our patrol
got attacked.

781
00:54:30,660 --> 00:54:34,907
That's easy. We're on a routine recon
inside Iraqi-controlled terrain.

782
00:54:35,123 --> 00:54:37,745
The patrol is ambushed.
RPG incoming, mortar fire.

783
00:54:37,959 --> 00:54:40,166
- You're knocked...
- Unconscious. Exactly the way...

784
00:54:40,379 --> 00:54:43,333
Not to cut you off, but I mean,
exactly the way that I remember it.

785
00:54:43,548 --> 00:54:46,336
But I dreamed something else.

786
00:54:47,970 --> 00:54:49,464
Am I in your dreams, captain?

787
00:54:50,389 --> 00:54:52,013
Yes, you are, congressman.

788
00:54:52,349 --> 00:54:53,464
Saving everybody?

789
00:54:53,684 --> 00:54:56,685
It's a whole lot more complicated
than that. Now, Corporal Melvin,

790
00:54:56,895 --> 00:54:59,495
he's been drawing these pictures
and he wrote down what he dreams.

791
00:54:59,565 --> 00:55:01,685
- Maybe if you just...
- I don't have dreams, captain.

792
00:55:02,401 --> 00:55:05,319
At all? You don't dream at all?
Everybody dreams, right? I mean...

793
00:55:05,529 --> 00:55:07,929
Look, captain, I'd like to help you,
I would, I really would,

794
00:55:08,074 --> 00:55:09,865
but I think you ought to
see somebody.

795
00:55:10,076 --> 00:55:12,276
- Somebody who specializes in...
- I've been to doctors.

796
00:55:12,620 --> 00:55:14,197
Well, good, that's very good,

797
00:55:14,413 --> 00:55:16,987
because they can probably
help you out a lot more than I can.

798
00:55:17,250 --> 00:55:18,970
- I don't know, but...
- Take care, captain.

799
00:55:19,085 --> 00:55:21,658
- Yeah. Yeah. Okay.
- Thanks for coming by.

800
00:55:28,136 --> 00:55:29,879
I'm not crazy, Shaw.

801
00:55:34,100 --> 00:55:35,642
Major.

802
00:55:37,854 --> 00:55:41,721
- Ben. Are you hungry?
- Starving.

803
00:55:47,405 --> 00:55:48,845
Well, it depends on the demographic.

804
00:55:49,032 --> 00:55:50,313
Excuse me.

805
00:55:51,827 --> 00:55:53,736
- I killed Baker?
- Well, it's a dream.

806
00:55:53,954 --> 00:55:56,077
I mean, it could mean
something else.

807
00:55:56,581 --> 00:55:58,907
It could mean I'm supposed
to think you did.

808
00:55:59,126 --> 00:56:02,958
No, I killed the enemy.
I didn't know them either, so...

809
00:56:03,338 --> 00:56:04,998
...it was okay.

810
00:56:05,758 --> 00:56:08,675
And anyway, I remember what we did
in Kuwait. I remember it perfectly.

811
00:56:08,886 --> 00:56:10,084
I just...

812
00:56:10,638 --> 00:56:13,045
...don't remember actually doing it.

813
00:56:13,807 --> 00:56:15,467
Maybe you didn't do it.

814
00:56:22,483 --> 00:56:23,977
No.

815
00:56:24,986 --> 00:56:26,563
What a thought.

816
00:56:44,672 --> 00:56:46,131
What?

817
00:56:50,929 --> 00:56:52,968
Life is so bizarre, isn't it?

818
00:56:54,015 --> 00:56:55,640
Which part?

819
00:56:55,850 --> 00:56:58,306
I don't know.
What you saw downstairs.

820
00:56:58,770 --> 00:57:04,690
This campaign. Politics.
My whole public life and persona.

821
00:57:06,236 --> 00:57:10,020
I mean, posing and grinning
like a goddamn sock puppet,

822
00:57:10,240 --> 00:57:12,910
shaking hands with total strangers
who must be completely blind

823
00:57:13,118 --> 00:57:15,490
if they can't see
what I am at the core.

824
00:57:15,704 --> 00:57:18,658
What my mother has made me.
A Prentiss.

825
00:57:18,874 --> 00:57:21,116
Ferociously a Prentiss.

826
00:57:21,710 --> 00:57:24,996
- But not a Shaw. No, sir.
- I see.

827
00:57:25,547 --> 00:57:27,125
No, you don't.

828
00:57:28,092 --> 00:57:29,290
You can't.

829
00:57:31,762 --> 00:57:33,719
I was 20 years old
before I had a friend.

830
00:57:33,931 --> 00:57:39,934
Worse, a girlfriend. Well, you know,
from my point of view, anyway.

831
00:57:40,313 --> 00:57:44,180
A friend outside of my mother's circle
of approved encounters

832
00:57:44,400 --> 00:57:46,523
and she...

833
00:57:48,905 --> 00:57:50,613
...my mother...

834
00:57:53,701 --> 00:57:58,162
God only knows what she told
Jocelyn to chase her away.

835
00:57:58,706 --> 00:58:01,328
Precipitating my sole act
of rebellion:

836
00:58:01,543 --> 00:58:03,370
Storming off...

837
00:58:04,170 --> 00:58:06,661
...and enlisting in the Army.

838
00:58:10,093 --> 00:58:11,504
But after the war...

839
00:58:13,513 --> 00:58:15,720
...I came back to her.

840
00:58:17,392 --> 00:58:19,551
Why did you come back?
What happened?

841
00:58:24,191 --> 00:58:25,982
Weren't you listening?

842
00:58:26,693 --> 00:58:28,651
Mother happened.

843
00:58:29,863 --> 00:58:32,070
You know, the truth is I hate it.

844
00:58:32,533 --> 00:58:34,821
I've always despised the Medal.

845
00:58:35,452 --> 00:58:38,786
The cloying adulation
of the little people.

846
00:58:39,790 --> 00:58:42,079
It's certainly...

847
00:58:42,334 --> 00:58:44,908
...nothing for you
to be jealous of, major.

848
00:58:45,129 --> 00:58:46,504
I'm not jealous.

849
00:58:47,465 --> 00:58:49,256
I don't have the dreams, Ben.

850
00:58:49,759 --> 00:58:54,088
How could you not remember
saving our unit?

851
00:58:54,680 --> 00:58:56,091
I do. I said I did.

852
00:58:56,307 --> 00:58:59,890
No, no, you didn't. You said
that you didn't remember doing it.

853
00:59:00,103 --> 00:59:02,428
That's what you just said
a couple minutes ago.

854
00:59:04,148 --> 00:59:06,355
When I think about that night...

855
00:59:07,986 --> 00:59:10,607
...it's as if I know what will happen.

856
00:59:11,865 --> 00:59:13,665
The thing is, I never seem
to get to the point

857
00:59:13,783 --> 00:59:16,986
where I feel that it actually
does happen.

858
00:59:17,203 --> 00:59:19,030
But I'm sure that's perfectly normal.

859
00:59:19,331 --> 00:59:22,949
Okay. Well, have you discussed this
with anyone? These discrepancies?

860
00:59:23,335 --> 00:59:25,493
Who would I share that with?

861
00:59:26,254 --> 00:59:28,627
My old Army buddies
who love and adore me

862
00:59:28,840 --> 00:59:30,963
for saving their
pathetically unimportant,

863
00:59:31,176 --> 00:59:33,632
present company excluded, asses?

864
00:59:34,096 --> 00:59:36,135
You could discuss it
with Army intelligence.

865
00:59:36,348 --> 00:59:39,764
You could go down there.
I mean, I could go with you

866
00:59:39,977 --> 00:59:42,137
and discuss it and you can tell them
what you remember,

867
00:59:42,354 --> 00:59:45,308
what you don't remember,
and they could...

868
00:59:46,066 --> 00:59:47,810
...run some tests.

869
00:59:50,571 --> 00:59:52,979
Yeah, tests. Boy.

870
00:59:53,199 --> 00:59:55,191
The press would have
a field day with that.

871
00:59:55,868 --> 00:59:58,573
Somebody put an implant inside me.
I found it this morning.

872
00:59:58,788 --> 01:00:01,148
I've got the hole in my back
if you wanna take a look at it.

873
01:00:01,207 --> 01:00:03,780
And I got a good feeling
they put one in you too.

874
01:00:09,841 --> 01:00:11,501
Nobody has put anything
in me, Ben.

875
01:00:11,717 --> 01:00:13,840
Let's prove it.
Why don't, you know...

876
01:00:14,053 --> 01:00:15,631
- We'll go get an x-ray...
- Look, Ben,

877
01:00:15,847 --> 01:00:17,638
I wanna be supportive of you. I do.

878
01:00:17,849 --> 01:00:20,422
But don't you think this could wait
till after the election?

879
01:00:20,643 --> 01:00:21,806
Why? For what?

880
01:00:22,020 --> 01:00:24,180
- What are you scared of?
- I'm not afraid of anything.

881
01:00:24,272 --> 01:00:27,223
- Then why don't we just prove it...
- Know what? I think you should leave.

882
01:00:27,233 --> 01:00:29,807
- I'm sorry, I really...
- Listen.

883
01:00:30,028 --> 01:00:34,820
Somebody got into our heads
with big steel-toe boots,

884
01:00:35,033 --> 01:00:37,489
cable cutters and a chainsaw
and they went to town.

885
01:00:37,702 --> 01:00:41,154
Neurons got... Got...
Got exposed and circuits got rewired.

886
01:00:41,373 --> 01:00:44,078
Our brain cells got
obliterated, Raymond.

887
01:00:44,292 --> 01:00:45,870
Please.

888
01:00:46,753 --> 01:00:48,711
You need to get help, Ben.

889
01:00:49,548 --> 01:00:51,754
What are you doing? Ben!

890
01:00:56,013 --> 01:00:57,721
Stop! Stop!

891
01:00:58,015 --> 01:00:59,213
Inside! Inside!

892
01:01:05,231 --> 01:01:06,226
Congressman!

893
01:01:12,113 --> 01:01:13,904
He bit him. He bit him.

894
01:01:18,369 --> 01:01:20,029
Get him out of here.

895
01:01:27,754 --> 01:01:29,331
Are you okay, sir?

896
01:01:31,966 --> 01:01:33,406
- Leave me alone.
- Sir, we should...

897
01:01:33,593 --> 01:01:35,135
Get out!

898
01:02:09,421 --> 01:02:11,129
We fished him out of
the Potomac River

899
01:02:11,340 --> 01:02:14,257
about 4:45 yesterday afternoon.

900
01:02:15,344 --> 01:02:18,215
What were you doing
in Al Melvin's apartment?

901
01:02:19,390 --> 01:02:20,932
I went to talk to him.
He wasn't home.

902
01:02:21,142 --> 01:02:24,143
Talk about what? Dreams?

903
01:02:27,064 --> 01:02:28,559
Interesting stuff.

904
01:02:28,774 --> 01:02:31,811
Yeah, there's hundreds
of those in his place.

905
01:02:32,028 --> 01:02:33,478
You should have your people
check it out.

906
01:02:33,488 --> 01:02:34,946
Oh, we'll get on that right away.

907
01:02:35,156 --> 01:02:38,490
Colonel Garret was kind enough
to show us the file on you, Marco.

908
01:02:38,701 --> 01:02:41,987
You are the real deal, aren't you?

909
01:02:43,248 --> 01:02:46,284
Special Forces. Rangers. Delta.

910
01:02:48,294 --> 01:02:50,038
I wanted to talk to Corporal Melvin

911
01:02:50,255 --> 01:02:54,122
to ask him some
unanswered questions about...

912
01:02:54,342 --> 01:02:57,012
...our reconnaissance
in Kuwait back in '91.

913
01:02:57,220 --> 01:02:59,047
- He wasn't home.
- Right. He wasn't there.

914
01:02:59,264 --> 01:03:02,799
So, what, you thought it was okay
to just break in and wait for him?

915
01:03:03,018 --> 01:03:04,676
I didn't kill him,
if that's where you're headed.

916
01:03:04,686 --> 01:03:06,346
Nobody said you did.

917
01:03:06,563 --> 01:03:08,022
Maybe he committed suicide.

918
01:03:10,108 --> 01:03:11,900
What's your obsession
with Raymond Shaw?

919
01:03:12,110 --> 01:03:13,688
I'm not obsessed
with Raymond Shaw.

920
01:03:13,904 --> 01:03:15,528
The man of his dreams.

921
01:03:17,074 --> 01:03:18,865
You may want to ask
your medical examiners

922
01:03:19,076 --> 01:03:20,950
to check Melvin's back.

923
01:03:21,161 --> 01:03:22,881
It's under the skin
just shy of the scapula.

924
01:03:23,038 --> 01:03:25,873
They may find a implant.

925
01:03:26,083 --> 01:03:27,708
Just under the skin, left side.

926
01:03:27,918 --> 01:03:30,160
If they don't look real hard,
they won't find it.

927
01:03:30,713 --> 01:03:33,193
They could sing that while
they're looking for it if they like.

928
01:03:33,257 --> 01:03:35,084
- Implants.
- That's what I said.

929
01:03:35,301 --> 01:03:36,961
I-M-plant.

930
01:03:37,178 --> 01:03:41,887
Yeah, but judging from
your file here, apparently,

931
01:03:42,099 --> 01:03:44,507
you don't know your shit
from your oatmeal, my friend.

932
01:03:44,727 --> 01:03:46,352
Excuse me. This is unnecessary.

933
01:03:47,104 --> 01:03:48,563
You got a problem?

934
01:03:49,649 --> 01:03:52,899
Psycho? You look a little angry.

935
01:03:54,112 --> 01:03:56,899
Maybe you wanna hit me?
Go ahead, you can do it.

936
01:03:58,074 --> 01:04:00,743
- Hey!
- For God's sake, Ben...

937
01:04:02,412 --> 01:04:03,443
He hit me.

938
01:04:04,748 --> 01:04:06,456
And you wanna help him?

939
01:04:06,666 --> 01:04:10,284
No. That would be political suicide.
Of course not.

940
01:04:10,795 --> 01:04:12,753
I want you to help him.

941
01:04:15,467 --> 01:04:18,634
I can't even imagine why.

942
01:04:19,388 --> 01:04:22,554
Mother, I can assure you, I am as
uncomfortable asking you to do this

943
01:04:22,766 --> 01:04:24,924
as you are being asked.

944
01:04:25,269 --> 01:04:27,842
My campaign people are getting
a restraining order against him.

945
01:04:28,063 --> 01:04:31,266
He's going on every security watch list,
but I won't lock him up.

946
01:04:31,483 --> 01:04:34,153
- I'm not pressing charges.
- What?

947
01:04:34,361 --> 01:04:36,520
I don't know, it's just...

948
01:04:40,117 --> 01:04:41,677
I don't wanna talk
about this right now.

949
01:04:41,744 --> 01:04:43,736
Can we get back to the campaign
and focus on something...

950
01:04:43,746 --> 01:04:47,115
Raymond, you don't actually
believe his story?

951
01:04:49,001 --> 01:04:50,828
No.

952
01:04:51,379 --> 01:04:53,455
But he does.

953
01:04:55,007 --> 01:04:57,463
And he's a fine soldier.

954
01:04:58,511 --> 01:05:01,216
And if his slim hold
on sanity requires

955
01:05:01,431 --> 01:05:03,951
that I tolerate his delusions
until he can get help, I'll do it.

956
01:05:04,100 --> 01:05:05,725
It doesn't diminish me.

957
01:05:06,352 --> 01:05:08,261
I'm not afraid of him.

958
01:05:09,397 --> 01:05:10,891
Raymond.

959
01:05:18,573 --> 01:05:22,156
How much do you actually know
about your friend?

960
01:05:53,651 --> 01:05:55,560
Oh, that's sad.

961
01:05:55,778 --> 01:05:57,687
Poor little tin soldier.

962
01:05:57,905 --> 01:05:59,565
Mother, please.

963
01:05:59,782 --> 01:06:02,355
Well, just imagine how terrified
your people were yesterday

964
01:06:02,576 --> 01:06:04,902
when Major Marco showed up
at campaign headquarters

965
01:06:05,121 --> 01:06:06,698
and you invite...

966
01:06:06,914 --> 01:06:09,037
My God, you invited him in.

967
01:06:09,667 --> 01:06:11,126
With all they know about him.

968
01:06:12,128 --> 01:06:14,037
I know him.

969
01:06:14,672 --> 01:06:16,629
I served under him.
He was a good man.

970
01:06:16,841 --> 01:06:20,044
Well, that's what the neighbors
